#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Un curs IBM gratuit despre informație și calcul cuantic"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products and projections"
msgstr "Produse interioare și proiecții"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"To better prepare ourselves to explore the capabilities and limitations of quantum circuits, we now introduce some additional mathematical concepts — namely the *inner product* between vectors (and its connection to the Euclidean norm), the notions of *orthogonality* and *orthonormality* for sets of vectors, and *projection* matrices, which will allow us to introduce a handy generalization of standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore Biggr, operatorname */}\n"
"Pentru a ne pregăti mai bine să explorăm capacitățile și limitările Circuit-urilor cuantice, introducem acum câteva concepte matematice suplimentare — și anume *produsul interior* dintre vectori (și legătura sa cu norma euclidiană), noțiunile de *ortogonalitate* și *ortonormalitate* pentru mulțimi de vectori, și matricele de *proiecție*, care ne vor permite să introducem o generalizare utilă a măsurătorilor în baze standard.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inner products {#inner-products}"
msgstr "Produse interioare {#inner-products}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recall that when we use the Dirac notation to refer to an arbitrary column vector as a ket, such as\n"
msgstr "Reamintim că atunci când folosim notația Dirac pentru a ne referi la un vector coloană arbitrar ca ket, de exemplu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "the corresponding bra vector is the *conjugate transpose* of this vector:\n"
msgstr "vectorul bra corespunzător este *transpusa conjugată* a acestui vector:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"=\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if we have some classical state set $\\Sigma$ in mind, and we express a column vector as a ket,\n"
"such as\n"
msgstr ""
"Alternativ, dacă avem în vedere o mulțime de stări clasice $\\Sigma$ și exprimăm un vector coloană ca ket,\n"
"de exemplu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then the corresponding row (or bra) vector is the conjugate transpose\n"
msgstr "atunci vectorul linie (sau bra) corespunzător este transpusa conjugată\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We also have that the product of a bra vector and a ket vector, viewed as matrices either having a single row or a single column, results in a scalar.\n"
"Specifically, if we have two column vectors\n"
msgstr ""
"De asemenea, produsul dintre un vector bra și un vector ket, privite ca matrice cu un singur rând sau o singură coloană, produce un scalar.\n"
"Concret, dacă avem doi vectori coloană\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_1\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so that the row vector $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is as in equation $(1)$, then\n"
msgstr "astfel încât vectorul linie $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ este cel din ecuația $(1)$, atunci\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_1} & \\overline{\\alpha_2} & \\cdots & \\overline{\\alpha_n}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\beta_1\\\\\n"
"\\beta_2\\\\\n"
"\\vdots\\\\\n"
"\\beta_n\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\beta_1 + \\cdots + \\overline{\\alpha_n}\\beta_n.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, if we have two column vectors that we have written as\n"
msgstr "Alternativ, dacă avem doi vectori coloană scriși ca\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so that $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ is the row vector $(2)$, we find that\n"
msgstr "astfel încât $\\langle \\psi \\vert$ este vectorul linie $(2)$, obținem că\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle & = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)\n"
"  \\Biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b\\rangle\\Biggr)\\\\\n"
"  & =\n"
"  \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_b \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the last equality follows from the observation that $\\langle a \\vert a \\rangle = 1$ and $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ for classical states $a$ and $b$ satisfying $a\\neq b$.\n"
msgstr "unde ultima egalitate decurge din observația că $\\langle a \\vert a \\rangle = 1$ și $\\langle a \\vert b \\rangle = 0$ pentru stările clasice $a$ și $b$ cu $a\\neq b$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The value $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ is called the *inner product* between the vectors $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Inner products are critically important in quantum information and computation;\n"
"we would not get far in understanding quantum information at a mathematical level without them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Valoarea $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle$ se numește *produsul interior* dintre vectorii $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ și $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$.\n"
"Produsele interioare sunt extrem de importante în informația și calculul cuantic;\n"
"nu am putea avansa prea mult în înțelegerea informației cuantice la nivel matematic fără ele.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us now collect together some basic facts about inner products of vectors.\n"
msgstr "Să adunăm acum câteva fapte de bază despre produsele interioare ale vectorilor.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Relationship to the Euclidean norm.** The inner product of any vector\n"
msgstr "**Relația cu norma euclidiană.** Produsul interior al oricărui vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   with itself is\n"
msgstr "   cu el însuși este\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\alpha_a\n"
"   = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert\\alpha_a\\vert^2\n"
"   = \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Thus, the Euclidean norm of a vector may alternatively be expressed as\n"
msgstr "   Astfel, norma euclidiană a unui vector poate fi exprimată alternativ ca\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\| \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| = \\sqrt{ \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle }.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Notice that the Euclidean norm of a vector must always be a nonnegative real number.\n"
"   Moreover, the only way the Euclidean norm of a vector can be equal to zero is if every one of the entries is equal to zero, which is to say that the vector is the zero vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Observă că norma euclidiană a unui vector trebuie să fie întotdeauna un număr real nenegativ.\n"
"   Mai mult, singurul mod în care norma euclidiană a unui vector poate fi egală cu zero este dacă fiecare intrare este egală cu zero, adică vectorul este vectorul nul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   We can summarize these observations like this: for every vector $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ we have\n"
msgstr "   Putem rezuma aceste observații astfel: pentru orice vector $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ avem\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\geq 0,\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   with $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ if and only if $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$.\n"
"   This property of the inner product is sometimes referred to as _positive definiteness_.\n"
msgstr ""
"   cu $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$ dacă și numai dacă $\\vert \\psi \\rangle = 0$.\n"
"   Această proprietate a produsului interior este uneori numită _definititudine pozitivă_.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Conjugate symmetry.** For any two vectors\n"
msgstr "**Simetrie conjugată.** Pentru oricare doi vectori\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\alpha_a \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\beta_b \\vert b \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   we have\n"
msgstr "   avem\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\alpha_a} \\beta_a\n"
"   \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"   \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\overline{\\beta_a} \\alpha_a,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   and therefore\n"
msgstr "   și prin urmare\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\overline{\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle} = \\langle \\phi \\vert \\psi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Linearity in the second argument (and conjugate linearity in the first).**\n"
"Let us suppose that $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$, $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle$, and $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers. If we define a new vector\n"
msgstr ""
"**Liniaritate în al doilea argument (și liniaritate conjugată în primul).**\n"
"Să presupunem că $\\vert \\psi \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle,$ și $\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle$ sunt vectori și $\\alpha_1$ și $\\alpha_2$ sunt numere complexe. Dacă definim un vector nou\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\phi\\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\phi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\phi_2\\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   then\n"
msgstr "   atunci\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   = \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigl( \\alpha_1\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"   = \\alpha_1 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   That is to say, the inner product is _linear_ in the second argument.\n"
"   This can be verified either through the formulas above or simply by noting that matrix multiplication is linear in each argument (and specifically in the second argument).\n"
msgstr ""
"   Cu alte cuvinte, produsul interior este _liniar_ în al doilea argument.\n"
"   Acest lucru poate fi verificat fie prin formulele de mai sus, fie observând pur și simplu că înmulțirea matriceală este liniară în fiecare argument (și în special în al doilea).\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Combining this fact with conjugate symmetry reveals that the inner product is _conjugate linear_ in the first argument. That is, if $\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle$, $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle$, and $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ are vectors and $\\alpha_1$ and $\\alpha_2$ are complex numbers, and we define\n"
msgstr "   Combinând acest fapt cu simetria conjugată, rezultă că produsul interior este _conjugat liniar_ în primul argument. Adică, dacă $\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle,$ $\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,$ și $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ sunt vectori și $\\alpha_1$ și $\\alpha_2$ sunt numere complexe, și definim\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\alpha_1 \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle + \\alpha_2 \\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle,\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\bigl( \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\bigr)\n"
"   \\vert\\phi\\rangle\n"
"   = \\overline{\\alpha_1} \\langle \\psi_1 \\vert \\phi \\rangle + \\overline{\\alpha_2} \\langle \\psi_2 \\vert \\phi \\rangle.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The Cauchy–Schwarz inequality.**\n"
"For every choice of vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ having the same number of entries, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"**Inegalitatea Cauchy–Schwarz.**\n"
"Pentru orice alegere de vectori $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ și $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ cu același număr de intrări, avem\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\bigl\\vert \\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle\\bigr| \\leq \\bigl\\| \\vert\\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\| \\bigl\\| \\vert \\phi \\rangle\n"
"   \\bigr\\|.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   This is an incredibly handy inequality that gets used quite extensively in quantum information (and in many other topics of study).\n"
msgstr "   Aceasta este o inegalitate extrem de utilă, folosită foarte frecvent în informația cuantică (și în multe alte domenii de studiu).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orthogonal and orthonormal sets {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"
msgstr "Mulțimi ortogonale și ortonormate {#orthogonal-and-orthonormal-sets}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two vectors $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ are said to be *orthogonal* if their inner product is zero:\n"
msgstr "Doi vectori $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ și $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ sunt numiți *ortogonali* dacă produsul lor interior este zero:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert \\phi \\rangle = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Geometrically, we can think about orthogonal vectors as vectors at right angles to each other.\n"
msgstr "Din punct de vedere geometric, putem să ne gândim la vectorii ortogonali ca la vectori care formează unghiuri drepte între ei.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthogonal set* if every vector in the set is orthogonal to every other vector in the set.\n"
"That is, this set is orthogonal if\n"
msgstr ""
"O mulțime de vectori $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ se numește *mulțime ortogonală* dacă fiecare vector din mulțime este ortogonal față de toți ceilalți vectori din mulțime.\n"
"Adică, această mulțime este ortogonală dacă\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle = 0\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ for which $j\\neq k$.\n"
msgstr "pentru orice alegere a lui $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$ cu $j\\neq k$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A set of vectors $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is called an *orthonormal* set if it is an orthogonal set and, in addition, every vector in the set is a unit vector.\n"
"Alternatively, this set is an orthonormal set if we have\n"
msgstr ""
"O mulțime de vectori $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ se numește *ortonormată* dacă este o mulțime ortogonală și, în plus, fiecare vector din mulțime este un vector unitar.\n"
"Alternativ, această mulțime este ortonormată dacă avem\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_j \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & j = k\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & j\\neq k\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\tag{3}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for all choices of $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$.\n"
msgstr "pentru orice alegere a lui $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,m\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, a set $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal basis* if, in addition to being an orthonormal set, it forms a basis.\n"
"This is equivalent to $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ being an orthonormal set and $m$ being equal to the dimension of the space from which $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"În fine, o mulțime $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ este o *bază ortonormată* dacă, pe lângă faptul că este o mulțime ortonormată, formează și o bază.\n"
"Acest lucru este echivalent cu faptul că $\\{ \\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ este o mulțime ortonormată și $m$ este egal cu dimensiunea spațiului din care sunt luați $\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, for any classical state set $\\Sigma$, the set of all standard basis vectors\n"
msgstr "De exemplu, pentru orice mulțime de stări clasice $\\Sigma$, mulțimea tuturor vectorilor bazei standard\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\big\\{ \\vert a \\rangle \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is an orthonormal basis.\n"
"The set $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $2$-dimensional space corresponding to a single qubit, and the Bell basis $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis for the $4$-dimensional space corresponding to two qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"este o bază ortonormată.\n"
"Mulțimea $\\{\\vert+\\rangle,\\vert-\\rangle\\}$ este o bază ortonormată pentru spațiul de dimensiune $2$ corespunzător unui singur Qubit, iar baza Bell $\\{\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\phi^-\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^+\\rangle, \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\}$ este o bază ortonormată pentru spațiul de dimensiune $4$ corespunzător a doi Qubiți.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extending orthonormal sets to orthonormal bases {#extending-orthonormal-sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"
msgstr "Extinderea mulțimilor ortonormate la baze ortonormate {#extending-orthonormal-sets-to-orthonormal-bases}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ are vectors that live in an $n$-dimensional space, and assume moreover that $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal set.\n"
"Orthonormal sets are always linearly independent sets, so these vectors necessarily span a subspace of dimension $m$.\n"
"From this we conclude that $m\\leq n$ because the dimension of the subspace spanned by these vectors cannot be larger than the dimension of the entire space from which they're drawn.\n"
msgstr ""
"Presupune că $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$ sunt vectori care aparțin unui spațiu $n$-dimensional și că $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ este o mulțime ortonormată.\n"
"Mulțimile ortonormate sunt întotdeauna mulțimi liniar independente, deci acești vectori generează în mod necesar un subspațiu de dimensiune $m$.\n"
"De aici concluzionăm că $m\\leq n$, deoarece dimensiunea subspațiului generat de acești vectori nu poate fi mai mare decât dimensiunea întregului spațiu din care sunt luați.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If it is the case that $m<n$, then it is always possible to choose an additional $n-m$ vectors\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ so that\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ forms an orthonormal basis.\n"
"A procedure known as the *Gram–Schmidt orthogonalization process* can be used to construct these vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dacă $m<n$, atunci este întotdeauna posibil să alegem încă $n-m$ vectori\n"
"$\\vert \\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ astfel încât\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ să formeze o bază ortonormată.\n"
"O procedură cunoscută sub numele de *procesul de ortonormare Gram–Schmidt* poate fi utilizată pentru a construi acești vectori.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Orthonormal sets and unitary matrices {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-matrices}"
msgstr "Mulțimi ortonormate și matrice unitare {#orthonormal-sets-and-unitary-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Orthonormal sets of vectors are closely connected with unitary matrices.\n"
"One way to express this connection is to say that the following three statements are logically equivalent (meaning that they are all true or all false) for any choice of a square matrix $U$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Mulțimile ortonormate de vectori sunt strâns legate de matricele unitare.\n"
"Un mod de a exprima această legătură este să spunem că următoarele trei afirmații sunt logic echivalente (adică fie toate sunt adevărate, fie toate sunt false) pentru orice alegere a unei matrice pătrate $U$:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The matrix $U$ is unitary (that is, $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U U^{\\dagger}$).\n"
msgstr "Matricea $U$ este unitară (adică, $U^{\\dagger} U = \\mathbb{I} = U U^{\\dagger}$).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The rows of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "Liniile lui $U$ formează o mulțime ortonormată.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The columns of $U$ form an orthonormal set.\n"
msgstr "Coloanele lui $U$ formează o mulțime ortonormată.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This equivalence is actually pretty straightforward when we think about how matrix multiplication and the conjugate transpose work.\n"
"Suppose, for instance, that we have a $3\\times 3$ matrix like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Această echivalență este de fapt destul de directă când ne gândim la modul în care funcționează înmulțirea matricelor și transpusa conjugată.\n"
"Presupune, de exemplu, că avem o matrice $3\\times 3$ de forma:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The conjugate transpose of $U$ looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Transpusa conjugată a lui $U$ arată astfel:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiplying the two matrices, with the conjugate transpose on the left-hand side, gives us this matrix:\n"
msgstr "Înmulțind cele două matrice, cu transpusa conjugată în stânga, obținem această matrice:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"&\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}} & \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1} & \\alpha_{1,2} & \\alpha_{1,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1} & \\alpha_{2,2} & \\alpha_{2,3} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1} & \\alpha_{3,2} & \\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\quad &=\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,1}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,1}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,1}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,2}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,2}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,2}}\\alpha_{3,3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,1} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,1} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,2} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,2} &\n"
"\\overline{\\alpha_{1,3}}\\alpha_{1,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{2,3}}\\alpha_{2,3} + \\overline{\\alpha_{3,3}}\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we form three vectors from the columns of $U$,\n"
msgstr "Dacă formăm trei vectori din coloanele lui $U$,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,1}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_2\\rangle = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,2}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"\\vert \\psi_3\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{1,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{2,3}\\\\\n"
"\\alpha_{3,3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then we can alternatively express the product above as follows:\n"
msgstr "atunci putem exprima alternativ produsul de mai sus astfel:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U^{\\dagger} U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_1\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_2\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_1 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_2 \\rangle & \\langle \\psi_3\\vert \\psi_3 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Referring to the equation $(3)$, we now see that the condition that this matrix is equal to the identity matrix is equivalent to the orthonormality of the set $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Referindu-ne la ecuația $(3)$, observăm acum că condiția ca această matrice să fie egală cu matricea identitate este echivalentă cu ortonormalitatea mulțimii $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_2\\rangle,\\vert\\psi_3\\rangle\\}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This argument generalizes to unitary matrices of any size.\n"
"The fact that the rows of a matrix form an orthonormal basis if and only if the matrix is unitary then follows from the fact that a matrix is unitary if and only if its transpose is unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Acest argument se generalizează la matrice unitare de orice dimensiune.\n"
"Faptul că liniile unei matrice formează o bază ortonormată dacă și numai dacă matricea este unitară rezultă din faptul că o matrice este unitară dacă și numai dacă transpusa sa este unitară.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the equivalence described above, together with the fact that every orthonormal set can be extended to form an orthonormal basis, we conclude the following useful fact:\n"
"Given any orthonormal set of vectors $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ drawn from an $n$-dimensional space, there exists a unitary matrix $U$ whose first $m$ columns are the vectors $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Pictorially, we can always find a unitary matrix having this form:\n"
msgstr ""
"Dat fiind echivalența descrisă mai sus, împreună cu faptul că orice mulțime ortonormată poate fi extinsă pentru a forma o bază ortonormată, concluzionăm următorul fapt util:\n"
"Dată orice mulțime ortonormată de vectori $\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ luați dintr-un spațiu $n$-dimensional, există o matrice unitară $U$ ale cărei prime $m$ coloane sunt vectorii $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_m\\rangle$.\n"
"Ilustrativ, putem găsi întotdeauna o matrice unitară de această formă:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\left(\n"
"  \\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\\\\\n"
"    \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_2\\rangle & \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_m\\rangle & \\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle &\n"
"    \\cdots & \\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"    \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt} & & \\rule{0.4pt}{10pt}\n"
"  \\end{array}\n"
"\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, the last $n-m$ columns are filled in with any choice of vectors $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ that make\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ an orthonormal basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aici, ultimele $n-m$ coloane sunt completate cu orice alegere de vectori $\\vert\\psi_{m+1}\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle$ care fac ca\n"
"$\\{\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_n\\rangle\\}$ să fie o bază ortonormată.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projections and projective measurements {#projections-and-projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Proiecții și măsurători proiective {#projections-and-projective-measurements}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projection matrices {#projection-matrices}"
msgstr "Matrice de proiecție {#projection-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A square matrix $\\Pi$ is called a *projection* if it satisfies two properties:\n"
msgstr "O matrice pătratică $\\Pi$ se numește *proiecție* dacă satisface două proprietăți:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '  1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}$.\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi = \\Pi^{\\dagger}$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '  2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi$.\n"
msgstr "$\\Pi^2 = \\Pi$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrices that satisfy the first condition — that they are equal to their own conjugate transpose — are called *Hermitian matrices*, and matrices that satisfy the second condition — that squaring them leaves them unchanged — are called *idempotent* matrices.\n"
msgstr "Matricele care satisfac prima condiție — că sunt egale cu transpusa lor conjugată — se numesc *matrice hermitiene*, iar matricele care satisfac a doua condiție — că ridicarea lor la pătrat le lasă nemodificate — se numesc matrice *idempotente*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a word of caution, the word *projection* is sometimes used to refer to any matrix that satisfies just the second condition but not necessarily the first, and when this is done the term *orthogonal projection* is typically used to refer to matrices satisfying both properties.\n"
"In the context of quantum information and computation, however, the terms *projection* and *projection matrix* more typically refer to matrices satisfying both conditions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ca o notă de precauție, cuvântul *proiecție* este uneori folosit pentru a se referi la orice matrice care satisface doar a doua condiție, dar nu neapărat și pe prima, și când se procedează astfel, termenul *proiecție ortogonală* este utilizat în mod tipic pentru a se referi la matricele care satisfac ambele proprietăți.\n"
"În contextul informației și calculului cuantic, totuși, termenii *proiecție* și *matrice de proiecție* se referă mai frecvent la matricele care satisfac ambele condiții.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An example of a projection is the matrix\n"
msgstr "Un exemplu de proiecție este matricea\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\n"
"\\tag{4}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for any unit vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"We can see that this matrix is Hermitian as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"pentru orice vector unitar $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$.\n"
"Putem vedea că această matrice este hermitiană astfel:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger} = \\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\bigl( \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\\bigl( \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, to obtain the second equality, we have used the formula\n"
msgstr "Aici, pentru a obține a doua egalitate, am folosit formula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(A B)^{\\dagger} = B^{\\dagger} A^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is always true, for any two matrices $A$ and $B$ for which the product $AB$ makes sense.\n"
msgstr "care este întotdeauna adevărată, pentru oricare două matrice $A$ și $B$ pentru care produsul $AB$ are sens.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see that the matrix $\\Pi$ in $(4)$ is idempotent, we can use the assumption that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a unit vector, so that it satisfies $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1$.\n"
"Thus, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Pentru a vedea că matricea $\\Pi$ din $(4)$ este idempotentă, putem folosi ipoteza că $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ este un vector unitar, astfel încât satisface $\\langle \\psi \\vert \\psi\\rangle = 1$.\n"
"Astfel, avem\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"= \\bigl( \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert \\bigr)^2\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"= \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert = \\Pi.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More generally, if $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ is any orthonormal set of vectors, then the matrix\n"
msgstr "Mai general, dacă $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ este orice mulțime ortonormată de vectori, atunci matricea\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{5}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a projection.\n"
"Specifically, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"este o proiecție.\n"
"Mai precis, avem\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^{\\dagger}\n"
"&= \\biggl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\bigl(\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert\\bigr)^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"&= \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"&= \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and\n"
msgstr "și\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Pi^2\n"
"& = \\biggl( \\sum_{j = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert\\Bigr)\\Bigl(\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{j = 1}^m\\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_j\\rangle \\langle \\psi_j \\vert  \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 1}^m \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\Pi,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where the orthonormality of $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implies the second-to-last equality.\n"
msgstr "unde ortonormalitatea lui $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$ implică penultima egalitate.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In fact, this exhausts all of the possibilities: *every* projection $\\Pi$ can be written in the form $(5)$ for some choice of an orthonormal set $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"(Technically speaking, the zero matrix $\\Pi=0$, which is a projection, is a special case.\n"
"To fit it into the general form $(5)$ we must allow the possibility that the sum is empty, resulting in the zero matrix.)\n"
msgstr ""
"De fapt, aceasta epuizează toate posibilitățile: *orice* proiecție $\\Pi$ poate fi scrisă în forma $(5)$ pentru o anumită alegere a unei mulțimi ortonormate $\\{\\vert \\psi_1\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert \\psi_m\\rangle\\}$.\n"
"(Tehnic vorbind, matricea zero $\\Pi=0$, care este o proiecție, este un caz special.\n"
"Pentru a o integra în forma generală $(5)$ trebuie să permitem posibilitatea ca suma să fie vidă, rezultând matricea zero.)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projective measurements {#projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Măsurători proiective {#projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The notion of a measurement of a quantum system is more general than just standard basis measurements.\n"
"*Projective measurements* are measurements that are described by a collection of projections whose sum is equal to the identity matrix.\n"
"In symbols, a collection $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ of projection matrices describes a projective measurement if\n"
msgstr ""
"Noțiunea de măsurătoare a unui sistem cuantic este mai generală decât simpla măsurătoare în baza standard.\n"
"*Măsurătorile proiective* sunt măsurători descrise de o colecție de proiecții a căror sumă este egală cu matricea identitate.\n"
"În termeni simbolici, o colecție $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ de matrice de proiecție descrie o măsurătoare proiectivă dacă\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When such a measurement is performed on a system $\\mathsf{X}$ while it is in some state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, two things happen:\n"
msgstr "Când o astfel de măsurătoare este efectuată asupra unui sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ aflat în starea $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, se întâmplă două lucruri:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, the outcome of the measurement is $k$ with probability equal to\n"
msgstr "Pentru fiecare $k\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, rezultatul măsurătorii este $k$ cu probabilitatea egală cu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{rezultatul este $k$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For whichever outcome $k$ the measurement produces, the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr "Pentru orice rezultat $k$ produs de măsurătoare, starea lui $\\mathsf{X}$ devine\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_k \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also choose outcomes other than $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ for projective measurements if we wish.\n"
"More generally, for any finite and nonempty set $\\Sigma$, if we have a collection of projection matrices\n"
msgstr ""
"Putem alege și alte rezultate decât $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ pentru măsurătorile proiective, dacă dorim.\n"
"Mai general, pentru orice mulțime finită și nevidă $\\Sigma$, dacă avem o colecție de matrice de proiecție\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_a:a\\in\\Sigma\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "that satisfies the condition\n"
msgstr "care satisface condiția\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\Pi_a = \\mathbb{I},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then this collection describes a projective measurement whose possible outcomes coincide with the set $\\Sigma$, where the rules are the same as before:\n"
msgstr "atunci această colecție descrie o măsurătoare proiectivă ale cărei rezultate posibile coincid cu mulțimea $\\Sigma$, unde regulile sunt aceleași ca înainte:\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $a\\in\\Sigma$, the outcome of the measurement is $a$ with probability equal to\n"
msgstr "Pentru fiecare $a\\in\\Sigma$, rezultatul măsurătorii este $a$ cu probabilitatea egală cu\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{outcome is $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl(\\text{rezultatul este $a$}\\bigr) = \\bigl\\| \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For whichever outcome $a$ the measurement produces, the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes\n"
msgstr "Pentru orice rezultat $a$ produs de măsurătoare, starea lui $\\mathsf{X}$ devine\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\|\\Pi_a \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\|}.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, standard basis measurements are equivalent to projective measurements, where $\\Sigma$ is the set of classical states of whatever system $\\mathsf{X}$ we're talking about and our set of projection matrices is\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"De exemplu, măsurătorile în baza standard sunt echivalente cu măsurătorile proiective, unde $\\Sigma$ este mulțimea stărilor clasice ale sistemului $\\mathsf{X}$ despre care vorbim, iar colecția de matrice de proiecție este\n"
"$\\{\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert:a\\in\\Sigma\\}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another example of a projective measurement, this time on two qubits $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$, is given by the set\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\}$, where\n"
msgstr ""
"Un alt exemplu de măsurătoare proiectivă, de această dată pe doi Qubiți $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$, este dat de mulțimea\n"
"$\\{\\Pi_0,\\Pi_1\\}$, unde\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 = \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\langle \\phi^+ \\vert + \\vert \\phi^-\\rangle\\langle \\phi^- \\vert + \\vert \\psi^+\\rangle\\langle \\psi^+ \\vert\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\Pi_1 = \\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we have multiple systems that are jointly in some quantum state and a projective measurement is performed on just one of the systems, the action is similar to what we had for standard basis measurements — and in fact we can now describe this action in much simpler terms than we could before.\n"
msgstr "Dacă avem mai multe sisteme care se află împreună într-o stare cuantică și o măsurătoare proiectivă este efectuată doar pe unul dintre sisteme, acțiunea este similară cu cea pe care am văzut-o pentru măsurătorile în baza standard — și de fapt acum putem descrie această acțiune în termeni mult mai simpli decât înainte.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be precise, let us suppose that we have two systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ in a quantum state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, and a projective measurement described by a collection $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ is performed on the system $\\mathsf{X}$, while nothing is done to $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Doing this is then equivalent to performing the projective measurement described by the collection\n"
msgstr ""
"Mai precis, să presupunem că avem două sisteme $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ într-o stare cuantică $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, iar o măsurătoare proiectivă descrisă de colecția $\\{\\Pi_a : a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ este efectuată asupra sistemului $\\mathsf{X}$, în timp ce asupra lui $\\mathsf{Y}$ nu se face nimic.\n"
"A face acest lucru este echivalent cu efectuarea măsurătorii proiective descrise de colecția\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\,:\\, a\\in\\Sigma\\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"on the joint system $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"Each measurement outcome $a$ results with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"pe sistemul comun $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$.\n"
"Fiecare rezultat al măsurătorii $a$ apare cu probabilitatea\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and conditioned on the result $a$ appearing, the state of the joint system $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ becomes\n"
msgstr "iar condiționat de apariția rezultatului $a,$ starea sistemului comun $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ devine\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{(\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| (\\Pi_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\\vert \\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementing projective measurements {#implementing-projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Implementarea măsurătorilor proiective {#implementing-projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Arbitrary projective measurements can be implemented using unitary operations, standard basis measurements, and an extra workspace system, as will now be explained.\n"
msgstr "Orice măsurătoare proiectivă poate fi implementată folosind operații unitare, măsurători în baza standard și un sistem de lucru suplimentar, după cum se va explica în cele ce urmează.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system and $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$. We can easily generalize this discussion to projective measurements having different sets of outcomes, but in the interest of convenience and simplicity we will assume the set of possible outcomes for our measurement is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Să presupunem că $\\mathsf{X}$ este un sistem și că $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ este o măsurătoare proiectivă pe $\\mathsf{X}$. Putem generaliza cu ușurință această discuție la măsurători proiective cu diferite mulțimi de rezultate, dar în interesul clarității și simplității vom presupune că mulțimea rezultatelor posibile ale măsurătorii noastre este $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us note explicitly that $m$ is not necessarily equal to the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ — we'll let $n$ be the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$, which means that each matrix $\\Pi_k$ is an $n\\times n$ projection matrix.\n"
msgstr "Să observăm explicit că $m$ nu trebuie să fie neapărat egal cu numărul de stări clasice ale lui $\\mathsf{X}$ — vom nota cu $n$ numărul de stări clasice ale lui $\\mathsf{X}$, ceea ce înseamnă că fiecare matrice $\\Pi_k$ este o matrice de proiecție $n\\times n$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because we assume that $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ represents a projective measurement, it is necessarily the case that\n"
msgstr "Deoarece presupunem că $\\{\\Pi_0\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ reprezintă o măsurătoare proiectivă, este în mod necesar adevărat că\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\Pi_k = \\mathbb{I}_n.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our goal is to perform a process that has the same effect as performing this projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$, but to do this using only unitary operations and standard basis measurements.\n"
msgstr "Scopul nostru este de a realiza un proces care are același efect ca efectuarea acestei măsurători proiective pe $\\mathsf{X}$, dar să facem acest lucru folosind doar operații unitare și măsurători în baza standard.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will make use of an extra workspace system $\\mathsf{Y}$ to do this, and specifically we'll take the classical state set of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to be $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, which is the same as the set of outcomes of the projective measurement.\n"
"The idea is that we will perform a standard basis measurement on $\\mathsf{Y}$, and interpret the outcome of this measurement as being equivalent to the outcome of the projective measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"We'll need to assume that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is initialized to some fixed state, which we'll choose to be $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"(Any other choice of fixed quantum state vector could be made to work, but choosing $\\vert 0\\rangle$ makes the explanation to follow much simpler.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Vom folosi un sistem de lucru suplimentar $\\mathsf{Y}$ pentru a face asta, și în mod specific vom lua mulțimea stărilor clasice ale lui $\\mathsf{Y}$ ca fiind $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, care coincide cu mulțimea rezultatelor măsurătorii proiective.\n"
"Ideea este că vom efectua o măsurătoare în baza standard pe $\\mathsf{Y}$ și vom interpreta rezultatul acestei măsurători ca echivalent cu rezultatul măsurătorii proiective pe $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Va trebui să presupunem că $\\mathsf{Y}$ este inițializat la o stare fixă, pe care o vom alege ca fiind $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"(Orice altă alegere a unui vector de stare cuantică fixă ar putea funcționa, dar alegerea $\\vert 0\\rangle$ face explicația ce urmează mult mai simplă.)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of course, in order for a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ to tell us anything about $\\mathsf{X}$, we will need to allow $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ to interact somehow before measuring $\\mathsf{Y}$, by performing a unitary operation on the system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$.\n"
"First consider this matrix:\n"
msgstr ""
"Desigur, pentru ca o măsurătoare în baza standard a lui $\\mathsf{Y}$ să ne spună ceva despre $\\mathsf{X}$, va trebui să permitem lui $\\mathsf{X}$ și $\\mathsf{Y}$ să interacționeze cumva înainte de a măsura $\\mathsf{Y}$, efectuând o operație unitară pe sistemul $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$.\n"
"Să considerăm mai întâi această matrice:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\Pi_k.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressed explicitly as a so-called *block matrix*, which is essentially a matrix of matrices that we interpret as a single, larger matrix, $M$ looks like this:\n"
msgstr "Exprimată explicit ca o așa-numită *matrice bloc*, care este în esență o matrice de matrice pe care o interpretăm ca o singură matrice mai mare, $M$ arată astfel:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, each $0$ represents an $n\\times n$ matrix filled entirely with zeros, so that the entire matrix $M$ is an $nm\\times nm$ matrix.\n"
msgstr "Aici, fiecare $0$ reprezintă o matrice $n\\times n$ umplută în întregime cu zerouri, astfel că întreaga matrice $M$ este o matrice $nm\\times nm.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, $M$ is certainly not a unitary matrix (unless $m=1$, in which case $\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I}$, giving $M = \\mathbb{I}$ in this trivial case) because unitary matrices cannot have any columns (or rows) that are entirely $0$; unitary matrices have columns that form orthonormal bases, and the all-zero vector is not a unit vector.\n"
msgstr "Acum, $M$ nu este cu siguranță o matrice unitară (cu excepția cazului $m=1,$ în care $\\Pi_0 = \\mathbb{I},$ dând $M = \\mathbb{I}$ în acest caz trivial) deoarece matricele unitare nu pot avea coloane (sau rânduri) cu totul zero; matricele unitare au coloane care formează baze ortonormate, iar vectorul zero nu este un vector unitar.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, it is the case that the first $n$ columns of $M$ are orthonormal, and we get this from the assumption that $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ is a measurement.\n"
"To verify this claim, notice that for each $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, the vector formed by column number $j$ of $M$ is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Totuși, este adevărat că primele $n$ coloane ale matricei $M$ sunt ortonormate, și deducem asta din presupunerea că $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ este o măsurătoare.\n"
"Pentru a verifica această afirmație, observă că pentru fiecare $j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$, vectorul format de coloana $j$ a lui $M$ este:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi_j\\rangle = M \\vert 0, j\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that here we're numbering the columns starting from column $0$. Taking the inner product of column $i$ with column $j$ when $i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ gives\n"
msgstr "Observă că numerotăm coloanele începând de la coloana $0$. Calculând produsul interior al coloanei $i$ cu coloana $j$ pentru $i,j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}$ obținem\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle \\psi_i \\vert \\psi_j \\rangle\n"
"& =\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert i\\rangle\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1} \\vert l \\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\biggr) \\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{l = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle k \\vert l \\rangle \\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_l \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1}\n"
"\\langle i \\vert \\Pi_k \\vert j\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\langle i \\vert \\mathbb{I} \\vert j \\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & i = j\\\\\n"
"0 & i\\neq j,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is what we needed to show.\n"
msgstr "ceea ce era de demonstrat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, because the first $n$ columns of the matrix $M$ are orthonormal, we can replace all of the remaining zero entries by some different choice of complex number entries so that the entire matrix is unitary.\n"
msgstr "Astfel, deoarece primele $n$ coloane ale matricei $M$ sunt ortonormate, putem înlocui toate intrările zero rămase cu alte valori ale numerelor complexe astfel încât întreaga matrice să fie unitară.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\Pi_0 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_1 & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\Pi_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we're given the matrices $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}$, we can compute suitable matrices to fill in for the blocks marked $\\fbox{?}$ in the equation — using the Gram–Schmidt process — but it does not matter specifically what these matrices are for the sake of this discussion.\n"
msgstr "Dacă ni se dau matricele $\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}$, putem calcula matrice potrivite pentru a umple blocurile marcate cu $\\fbox{?}$ din ecuație — folosind procesul Gram–Schmidt — dar nu contează specific ce anume sunt aceste matrice în scopul acestei discuții.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally we can describe the measurement process: we first perform $U$ on the joint system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ and then measure $\\mathsf{Y}$ with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"For an arbitrary state $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ of $\\mathsf{X}$, we obtain the state\n"
msgstr ""
"În final putem descrie procesul de măsurătoare: mai întâi aplicăm $U$ pe sistemul comun $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ și apoi măsurăm $\\mathsf{Y}$ printr-o măsurătoare în baza standard.\n"
"Pentru o stare arbitrară $\\vert \\phi \\rangle$ a lui $\\mathsf{X}$, obținem starea\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= M \\bigl( \\vert 0\\rangle \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\Pi_k \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the first equality follows from the fact that $U$ and $M$ agree on their first $n$ columns.\n"
"When we perform a projective measurement on $\\mathsf{Y}$, we obtain each outcome $k$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"unde prima egalitate decurge din faptul că $U$ și $M$ coincid pe primele $n$ coloane ale lor.\n"
"Când efectuăm o măsurătoare proiectivă pe $\\mathsf{Y}$, obținem fiecare rezultat $k$ cu probabilitatea\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|^2,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ becomes\n"
msgstr "caz în care starea lui $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ devine\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert k\\rangle \\otimes \\frac{\\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle}{\\bigl\\| \\Pi_k \\vert \\phi\\rangle \\bigr\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, $\\mathsf{Y}$ stores a copy of the measurement outcome and $\\mathsf{X}$ changes precisely as it would had the projective measurement described by $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ been performed directly on $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr "Astfel, $\\mathsf{Y}$ stochează o copie a rezultatului măsurătorii, iar $\\mathsf{X}$ se modifică exact cum s-ar fi modificat dacă măsurătoarea proiectivă descrisă de $\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}$ ar fi fost efectuată direct pe $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
